# Owner-domain reads: a subsystem's own thread reading its own
# pointer-stable singleton. The video thread and ra-video's state is
# the design; the audit holds everything else to published snapshots,
# latched fields, or arguments captured when the work was posted.
video_thread_loop|video_state_get_ptr
# runloop_msg_queue_push() defers an off-main caller before touching
# anything: the worker's message waits under the message queue lock
# for the main thread's iterate to replay it. Its widget, font,
# accessibility and settings work therefore happens on the main
# thread for every caller.
@boundary runloop_msg_queue_push
# task_load_handler polls video frame_count once per tick to hold the
# load until the core has rendered (Dolphin CLI): a single benign
# read of a monotonic counter, documented at the site - the old code
# spun on it, which the comment there explains. No settings coherence
# is at stake and no progress depends on observing it promptly.
task_load_handler|video_state_get_ptr
